course: dictionary
lesson: 7163
title: Peripheral: the edges and the extras
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Peripheral means at the edge or outside part of something, not in the middle. «Side vision (peripheral vision) is good at spotting movement but poor at seeing detail.» Here peripheral vision is what you see at the sides, not what you look at directly.
explain: Peripheral can also mean less important, not the main part. A peripheral issue is a small problem that is not the heart of the matter. To check, ask yourself: is this at the edge, or is it at the centre?
explain: Peripheral is also a noun. A peripheral is an extra device you connect to a computer, like a mouse, keyboard or printer. So the printer is a peripheral, not the main computer itself.
fact: Peripheral means at the edge or outside part of something, not in the middle.
fact: Peripheral vision is what you see at the sides without turning your head.
fact: Peripheral vision is good at spotting movement but poor at seeing detail.
fact: A peripheral issue is a less important problem, not the main one.
fact: A peripheral is an extra device you connect to a computer, such as a mouse, keyboard, printer, scanner or headphones.
exercise: «Side vision (peripheral vision) is good at spotting movement.» What does peripheral mean in this sentence? | Hidden under the floor | Very loud | In the very centre | *At the edge, to the side
exercise: The teacher said the scratch on the desk was a peripheral issue, and the lost homework was the main problem. What does peripheral issue mean? | A big problem that must be solved first | A problem at the very centre of the lesson | A problem with the weather | *A less important problem
exercise: Which one is a peripheral? | The middle of a road | A window in the classroom | A pencil case | *A keyboard connected to a computer
test: Which phrase means what you see at the sides without turning your head? | Central vision | Night vision | Blurred vision | *Peripheral vision
test: Mia said the spilled paint was peripheral to the main problem. What does peripheral mean here? | Brand new | Blue | *Less important | Very big
exam: Why is peripheral vision useful when you cross the road? | To see only the middle of the road | *To spot cars moving at the sides without turning your head | To read the road signs in fine detail | To hear the horn from far away
